Write short comparison table: SOC analyst day-to-day VS jnr pen-tester day-to-day

SOC analyst	
Goals
Detect, contain and eradicate active attacks or suspicious behaviour in the network.
Triage and investigate security alerts, isolate infected hosts, conduct proactive threat hunting.

Tools
SIEM and EDR would be crucial to detecting anomalies.
Network and Forensic Analysis through tools such as Wireshark.

Success measure
How quickly malicious behaviour is recognized and contained in the network.
The ability to filter out noise and false positives without missing true positives.
Writing and defining detection signatures.

Risk
Shift unpredictability and alert fatigue


Junior Penetration Tester
Goals	
Uncover hidden vulnerabilities, prove exploitation impacts, and help patch gaps before a real attack.
Reconnaissance and OSINT on targets, simulate real-world attack chains, retest fixes after remediation.

Tools	
The holy trinity of pentesting refers to Nmap, Burp Suite and Metasploit. 
Custom scripts can also be used for exploitation.

Success measure	
Severity and impact of findings based on how they can negatively affect the organisation.
Report quality and clarity paired with proof of concept are important.

Risk	
Deadline and delivery pressure
Breaking production server mid-test

5 bullets on how AI could help after enumeration and what you would still do by hand

  •	Automated data cleaning which rapidly identifies and fixes formatting errors. Data can be verified by analysts to create contextual understanding
  •	Advanced pattern recognition through machine learning to detect hidden trends and anomalies that humans may miss. People can be given the responsibility of ensuring data integrity and accuracy.
  •	Predictive forecasting can be used to project future resource needs and demands. Humans will be responsible for presenting data to clients and boards to build trust and get assistance.
  •	Generative AI can instantly translate complex raw data into readable reports or summaries. Humans will be responsible for strategic decision making based on data findings.
  •	AI can automatically tag and group unstructured notes which humans can then review to maintain ethical responsibility and ensure there is no biased output of assumptions.
 
